  "description": "Test-only keypairs (Ed25519, ES256, RS256) for ARSIA Protocol test vectors. NOT secrets. The six Ed25519 keypairs added in the vector cycle are derived deterministically: private key = SHA-256 of the UTF-8 string 'arsia-test-vectors keypair ' followed by the agent-id; kid = agent-id + '#key1'. Two Ed25519 keypairs added in coverage SC1 are derived from the kid: private key = SHA-256 of the UTF-8 string 'arsia-test-vectors keypair ' followed by the kid. An agent's first key is indexed by its agent-id; an additional key of the same agent is indexed by its kid (agent:acme.echo-client#other-key), so the existing entries are unchanged. Draft-01.1 port: 34 entries are imported unchanged from origin/main 17dcf33 (the Draft-01.1 test keys), only those whose kid a Draft-02 vector uses and this catalog lacked; the main reconciliation imports one more under the same rule, agent:acme.state-extension#key1 for ITV-266 (35 imported in all); an existing entry is never overwritten, and the five kids whose public key differs between the two catalogs keep their Draft-02 key. Two keys no catalog had are generated: agent:contoso.crm#key1 (Ed25519, derived from the kid as the coverage SC1 keys) and agent:acme.legacy-system#rsa1024, an RSA key of 1024 bits deliberately BELOW the 2048-bit minimum of ARSIA-Core.md §5.1, which exists only for the key-size negative ITV-425 and must never verify. The provenance member records the three sets and their digests.",
